1
00:00:07,960 --> 00:00:10,000
I'm giving you one last extension.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,880
Or I'll shut down your research lab.

3
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:13,680
Say ahhhh.

4
00:00:13,840 --> 00:00:15,040
You're teasing me, Gen!

5
00:00:15,120 --> 00:00:17,280
If there were two people
who looked exactly alike,

6
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:19,280
who would you choose to be with, Gen?

7
00:00:19,360 --> 00:00:20,360
I choose you.

8
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:28,480
Ai is the most perfect artificial
intelligence we've ever created,

9
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:30,960
and the investor wants her back.

10
00:00:31,160 --> 00:00:33,880
Even if you refuse,
you can't fight them.

11
00:00:47,360 --> 00:00:48,120
Ai?

12
00:00:48,640 --> 00:00:49,840
I’m sorry, Ai.

13
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:52,320
But I'm not letting those people take you back.

14
00:01:55,960 --> 00:01:58,640
A382's expressions are remarkably human.

15
00:02:00,520 --> 00:02:01,560
Too human, if you ask me.

16
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:07,240
Did you get it?

17
00:02:14,920 --> 00:02:15,920
Does Irene know?

18
00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:17,120
No, sir.

19
00:02:17,160 --> 00:02:20,040
Khun Irene doesn't know we have
a backup shutdown key for A382.

20
00:02:20,520 --> 00:02:22,480
Good thing you had us make one.

21
00:02:26,480 --> 00:02:28,560
We're really not going to
tell Khun Irene about this?

22
00:02:31,160 --> 00:02:31,800
No.

23
00:02:32,640 --> 00:02:33,960
She's too soft-hearted.

24
00:02:36,120 --> 00:02:37,280
And that soft heart of hers…

25
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:40,280
will be the end of us all.

26
00:02:52,120 --> 00:02:53,160
I'll take responsibility.

27
00:02:53,960 --> 00:02:56,079
It is my duty to protect this research center.

28
00:02:56,760 --> 00:02:57,760
And so is yours...

29
00:02:59,160 --> 00:03:00,160
Irene's too.

30
00:03:00,880 --> 00:03:05,240
You know what will happen if we don't
have a product to deliver, don't you?

31
00:03:06,760 --> 00:03:10,720
Everything we've worked so hard on
for all these years will be for nothing.

32
00:03:12,360 --> 00:03:13,600
You understand that, don't you?

33
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:37,440
So, did you find one or not?

34
00:05:38,240 --> 00:05:42,040
Of course. It's just a place to stay
in London. I can handle that for you.

35
00:05:42,480 --> 00:05:46,000
But Gen... why did you
say this had to be a secret?

36
00:05:46,640 --> 00:05:49,840
I mean, yes, I can get you
a place under another name,

37
00:05:50,159 --> 00:05:52,040
and P' Le already said she'd help.

38
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:55,960
But can you at least tell me
what exactly you're doing?

39
00:05:58,520 --> 00:06:00,320
I'll tell you everything once this is over.

40
00:06:01,120 --> 00:06:02,480
Are you getting back at me?

41
00:06:04,360 --> 00:06:07,320
You literally hid from me that
you died and traveled back in time.

42
00:06:08,360 --> 00:06:12,080
Fine, I get it. I doubt your story could
be any more fantastical than mine.

43
00:06:12,480 --> 00:06:14,480
But you have to tell me once this is all over.

44
00:06:15,280 --> 00:06:16,040
Mm.

45
00:06:24,680 --> 00:06:25,720
Fantasy? No.

46
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:28,160
But sci-fi? Definitely.

47
00:06:37,120 --> 00:06:38,000
What are you doing?

48
00:06:39,840 --> 00:06:40,680
Don't look.

49
00:06:41,040 --> 00:06:42,960
What? Why can't I look?

50
00:06:44,159 --> 00:06:47,520
No means no. You took your
phone back from me before too.

51
00:06:47,800 --> 00:06:49,960
I had to talk about something important.

52
00:06:51,080 --> 00:06:52,680
This is important to me too.

53
00:06:56,040 --> 00:06:57,600
So you're really not going to tell me?

54
00:06:59,320 --> 00:07:00,320
I'm not telling you.

55
00:07:00,800 --> 00:07:02,360
And you can't ask me about it either.

56
00:07:02,520 --> 00:07:04,920
Sometimes, people need to
keep secrets from each other.

57
00:07:05,080 --> 00:07:08,200
Wanting to know everything can
lead to arguments between couples.

58
00:07:08,760 --> 00:07:10,480
And I don't want to argue with you, Gen.

59
00:07:10,920 --> 00:07:13,360
That's why you can't ask me about it.

60
00:07:20,560 --> 00:07:21,920
So, are we a couple now?

61
00:07:24,440 --> 00:07:25,640
Aren't we?

62
00:07:26,840 --> 00:07:27,840
What do you think?

63
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:31,600
We hug...

64
00:07:33,360 --> 00:07:34,080
we kiss...

65
00:07:36,440 --> 00:07:37,440
and we have sex—

66
00:07:37,720 --> 00:07:38,560
Too blunt!

67
00:07:40,400 --> 00:07:41,560
But isn't that true?

68
00:07:46,280 --> 00:07:53,360
You know, just because
we hug, kiss, or... have sex

69
00:07:54,880 --> 00:07:56,600
doesn't always mean we're a couple.

70
00:07:57,320 --> 00:07:59,240
Don't you have that
information in your database?

71
00:08:04,200 --> 00:08:06,280
You're the worst.

72
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:11,600
Hey! You actually called me that?

73
00:08:12,040 --> 00:08:14,400
Ai, come back and talk to me right now.

74
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:15,880
Ai!

75
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:17,720
Ai.

76
00:08:18,240 --> 00:08:19,760
Talk to me.

77
00:08:20,840 --> 00:08:21,840
I'm not talking!

78
00:08:22,080 --> 00:08:23,120
Don't be like that.

79
00:08:23,200 --> 00:08:25,000
Do I have to listen just because you said so?

80
00:08:26,440 --> 00:08:28,200
You're becoming more like a human, you know.

81
00:08:28,360 --> 00:08:29,640
You don't like that?

82
00:08:30,120 --> 00:08:33,960
You told me not to use my database.
You didn't like me analyzing things.

83
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:38,000
You said using facial recognition was wrong,
and told me to learn human emotions instead.

84
00:08:38,039 --> 00:08:40,159
And now that I do,
you say I'm becoming human.

85
00:08:40,720 --> 00:08:45,720
Then should I go back to being
an emotionless robot, Master?

86
00:08:46,360 --> 00:08:47,920
I never said I didn't like it.

87
00:08:50,080 --> 00:08:54,080
Stop teasing me.
I'm not a one-month-old robot anymore.

88
00:09:00,520 --> 00:09:01,480
I like it.

89
00:09:04,240 --> 00:09:05,240
I like you.

90
00:09:16,120 --> 00:09:19,000
Wait, what? I tell you
the truth and you run away?

91
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:20,360
Don't follow me.

92
00:09:20,400 --> 00:09:22,320
I'm going to follow you.
Who's going to stop me?

93
00:09:22,720 --> 00:09:23,600
Ai!

94
00:09:24,760 --> 00:09:25,520
Don't go.

95
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:30,400
Gotcha!

96
00:09:35,600 --> 00:09:36,200
Ai!

97
00:09:36,880 --> 00:09:39,000
Where are you? Hey!

98
00:09:45,720 --> 00:09:46,440
Ai!

99
00:09:47,560 --> 00:09:48,360
Stop!

100
00:09:50,520 --> 00:09:52,400
- You can't get away this time.
- Not a chance.

101
00:09:52,600 --> 00:09:53,480
Try me.

102
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:07,240
See? Told you I’d catch you.

103
00:10:10,400 --> 00:10:13,000
My master is so mean.

104
00:10:20,360 --> 00:10:21,800
I’m not your master.

105
00:10:26,320 --> 00:10:27,520
I’m your partner.

106
00:10:30,560 --> 00:10:32,040
Your girlfriend, you know?

107
00:10:41,960 --> 00:10:43,600
Can you say that again, Gen?

108
00:10:44,680 --> 00:10:45,480
Say what?

109
00:10:47,960 --> 00:10:49,640
The part where you said...

110
00:10:49,960 --> 00:10:50,920
I love you.

111
00:11:02,840 --> 00:11:06,360
~ Now I know that good love looks just like you ~

112
00:11:06,400 --> 00:11:09,320
~ I’m glad that we found each other ~

113
00:11:09,360 --> 00:11:13,520
~ Your love feels like a dream ~

114
00:11:13,560 --> 00:11:16,840
~ Whatever tomorrow may bring ~

115
00:11:16,840 --> 00:11:19,080
~ Whether it’s good or bad ~

116
00:11:19,120 --> 00:11:23,520
~ As long as I have you, it will be alright ~

117
00:11:23,520 --> 00:11:26,640
~ Because you understand me ~

118
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:44,120
You know what, Gen?

119
00:11:45,120 --> 00:11:45,840
What?

120
00:11:48,240 --> 00:11:49,600
You like holding my cheeks.

121
00:11:54,360 --> 00:11:55,240
Like this?

122
00:11:58,600 --> 00:12:00,040
This is called pinching.

123
00:12:03,240 --> 00:12:04,840
And this is called a peck.

124
00:12:07,800 --> 00:12:09,040
You're really mischievous.

125
00:12:09,760 --> 00:12:11,680
Wanna know what "really mischievous" looks like?

126
00:12:12,640 --> 00:12:13,600
C'mere.

127
00:12:16,600 --> 00:12:18,080
I give in.

128
00:12:27,040 --> 00:12:30,920
So... have you ever been to England before, Gen?

129
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:37,480
No, I haven't.
I've only heard about it from my friend.

130
00:12:38,640 --> 00:12:41,400
My friend studied in England,
but she’s back now.

131
00:12:42,080 --> 00:12:43,960
I’ll introduce you to her if we get the chance.

132
00:12:47,960 --> 00:12:49,920
So what are we going to do there?

133
00:12:51,360 --> 00:12:52,360
I don't know.

134
00:12:55,080 --> 00:12:56,160
I don't really have a plan.

135
00:12:59,480 --> 00:13:00,360
Surprised?

136
00:13:04,360 --> 00:13:05,720
I'm surprised at myself too.

137
00:13:10,040 --> 00:13:13,600
I used to be the kind of person who planned
everything, who worried about everything.

138
00:13:15,840 --> 00:13:17,560
I'd worry about whether I'd find a job,

139
00:13:18,480 --> 00:13:19,520
whether I'd be okay,

140
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:21,880
what my mom would think...

141
00:13:24,080 --> 00:13:25,960
Suddenly, I don't want
to plan anything at all.

142
00:13:27,720 --> 00:13:29,480
I'll be honest with you...

143
00:13:31,680 --> 00:13:36,200
when we get there,
I'm not even sure if we'll make it.

144
00:13:37,720 --> 00:13:41,000
Even though I have some savings,

145
00:13:42,960 --> 00:13:47,720
if I can't find a job... I honestly
don't know what I'd do next.

146
00:13:56,400 --> 00:13:57,920
It's all because of me.

147
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:06,080
It's because of me.

148
00:14:09,760 --> 00:14:11,280
Because I want to be with you.

149
00:14:23,400 --> 00:14:24,480
Gen…

150
00:14:26,880 --> 00:14:28,280
Let's start a new life together.

151
00:14:30,280 --> 00:14:31,280
Just the two of us.

152
00:14:45,560 --> 00:14:48,080
I never wanted you to go
through all this because of me.

153
00:14:49,880 --> 00:14:51,120
Don't say that.

154
00:14:57,880 --> 00:14:59,560
But I don't want to go back to the lab.

155
00:15:02,120 --> 00:15:04,000
I don't want to live my life analyzing things.

156
00:15:04,920 --> 00:15:06,320
I don't want to be just a machine.

157
00:15:09,320 --> 00:15:10,800
I don't want to become someone else.

158
00:15:22,600 --> 00:15:23,600
Most importantly...

159
00:15:25,600 --> 00:15:27,000
I don’t want to forget.

160
00:15:39,240 --> 00:15:40,240
You won’t forget.

161
00:15:47,320 --> 00:15:48,880
I'm afraid I'll forget you.

162
00:15:53,760 --> 00:15:55,880
I'm afraid they'll erase all my memories.

163
00:16:02,200 --> 00:16:03,400
And I’m afraid…

164
00:16:06,280 --> 00:16:10,280
I'm afraid I'll forget who you are.

165
00:16:14,840 --> 00:16:17,480
Even though you're the
most important person to me.

166
00:16:37,200 --> 00:16:38,200
You won't forget.

167
00:16:40,160 --> 00:16:41,160
I promise.

168
00:17:02,040 --> 00:17:04,319
Now that you know how to cry,
you really don't hold back.

169
00:17:06,079 --> 00:17:08,560
Because I know you'll comfort me.

170
00:17:11,880 --> 00:17:14,920
Mm. I’ll comfort you.

171
00:17:25,440 --> 00:17:26,760
I love you.

172
00:17:42,040 --> 00:17:45,200
You see, a shadow is created by the light source.

173
00:17:45,600 --> 00:17:50,400
The closer the light is to the object,
the stronger the shadow becomes.

174
00:17:50,800 --> 00:17:52,520
Take this vase, for example.

175
00:17:53,120 --> 00:17:55,560
Let’s say the light is coming
from this direction, right?

176
00:17:55,600 --> 00:17:57,280
The shadow will always fall this way.

177
00:17:57,560 --> 00:17:59,200
And when we shade shadows like this,

178
00:17:59,880 --> 00:18:02,160
the intensity doesn't always have to be even.

179
00:18:03,400 --> 00:18:04,320
Do you get it?

180
00:18:07,160 --> 00:18:08,880
Theoretically, yes.

181
00:18:13,760 --> 00:18:15,480
You have to practice too.

182
00:18:15,520 --> 00:18:17,320
Knowing the theory doesn't mean you can draw.

183
00:18:17,680 --> 00:18:19,200
Alright, give it a try.

184
00:18:22,720 --> 00:18:23,880
Look at the vase.

185
00:18:24,920 --> 00:18:26,480
Yeah, like that.

186
00:18:27,400 --> 00:18:28,840
Blend the shades from dark to light.

187
00:18:35,280 --> 00:18:37,360
It's P' Ploy.
Keep drawing, okay?

188
00:18:42,240 --> 00:18:45,360
Come see me at the office.

189
00:18:50,320 --> 00:18:53,720
You come to me instead.
You know I'm in hiding.

190
00:18:53,720 --> 00:18:56,360
I can't. I need to talk to you
about something important.

191
00:18:57,480 --> 00:18:58,680
What about?

192
00:18:58,720 --> 00:19:02,600
That robot.
Hurry. It's urgent.

193
00:19:06,680 --> 00:19:08,200
Why is P' Ploy calling Ai a robot?

194
00:19:18,240 --> 00:19:20,520
Ai, I have to go out for a bit.

195
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:22,000
Where are you going?

196
00:19:22,360 --> 00:19:24,640
It’s P’ Ploy.
She said she has some work for me.

197
00:19:31,640 --> 00:19:33,240
Don’t worry. I won’t be long.

198
00:19:35,560 --> 00:19:36,800
Can you stay here by yourself?

199
00:19:37,720 --> 00:19:38,720
Yes.

200
00:19:41,320 --> 00:19:42,800
Come back soon, okay, Gen?

201
00:19:46,080 --> 00:19:47,800
Has anyone ever told you that you're cute?

202
00:19:50,440 --> 00:19:53,640
Would you be mad if someone else did?

203
00:19:55,400 --> 00:19:56,960
You look like you want me to get mad.

204
00:20:01,080 --> 00:20:03,080
I’ll hurry back and check your homework, student.

205
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:10,080
Is something wrong, miss?

206
00:21:11,800 --> 00:21:14,160
Oh, no. It's nothing.

207
00:21:14,400 --> 00:21:17,800
You kept looking around, so I thought
you were running from someone.

208
00:21:18,200 --> 00:21:21,160
Look, I don't wanna brag,
but I'm gonna say it anyway.

209
00:21:21,400 --> 00:21:23,680
I might not look it, but I'm a speed demon.

210
00:21:23,880 --> 00:21:25,800
Running from your husband?
Got your mother-in-law after you?

211
00:21:25,840 --> 00:21:27,720
I’ll put the pedal to the metal.
Sound good?

212
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:31,720
I believe in getting to my destination safely.

213
00:21:32,200 --> 00:21:33,360
No need to rush, please.

214
00:21:44,120 --> 00:21:46,400
What is it now?
I’m already on my way.

215
00:21:46,680 --> 00:21:49,440
What? Where are you going?
Who are you meeting?

216
00:21:49,520 --> 00:21:52,440
Are you crazy, going
out at a time like this?

217
00:21:53,920 --> 00:21:54,840
P' Ploy?

218
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:58,160
Of course! Who else would it be?
So where are you going?

219
00:21:58,440 --> 00:22:00,360
Hey, are you messing with me?

220
00:22:00,520 --> 00:22:03,160
You asked me to come meet
you, and now you’re asking me?

221
00:22:03,520 --> 00:22:06,360
Starting to get Alzheimer’s?
Go get yourself checked when you have time.

222
00:22:06,480 --> 00:22:09,440
Hey, I don't have Alzheimer's.
You and that mouth of yours.

223
00:22:09,840 --> 00:22:13,240
Then who asked you to come out?
Don’t be crazy. It wasn’t me!

224
00:22:13,640 --> 00:22:16,120
I was calling to tell you I lost my phone.

225
00:22:16,160 --> 00:22:17,640
If you need me, call this number.

226
00:22:17,840 --> 00:22:21,400
So where are you going? Didn’t Khun Irene
tell you to keep a low profile for now?

227
00:22:22,360 --> 00:22:24,120
Are you listening to me, Gen?

228
00:22:24,120 --> 00:22:26,360
Sir! Sir! Turn back the way we came!

229
00:22:26,760 --> 00:22:28,080
What’s with you all of a sudden?

230
00:22:28,360 --> 00:22:30,840
Come on! Speed demon, speed
monster, speed goblin, whatever!

231
00:22:30,880 --> 00:22:33,120
Just turn back the way we came now! Now!

232
00:22:37,560 --> 00:22:39,240
You got it!

233
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:03,880
Let’s go.

234
00:23:25,240 --> 00:23:28,680
Humans are very emotionally complex beings.

235
00:23:28,960 --> 00:23:30,240
Can you teach me?

236
00:23:30,520 --> 00:23:36,240
I want to know what anger, pain,
despair, excitement, happiness,

237
00:23:36,600 --> 00:23:38,560
or loving someone feel like.

238
00:23:38,720 --> 00:23:39,960
Can you teach me, Gen?

239
00:23:40,240 --> 00:23:41,280
Why me?

240
00:23:42,280 --> 00:23:45,120
I... want you to be the one to teach me.

241
00:23:48,280 --> 00:23:51,800
You call what just happened
an “exchange of oral fluids”?

242
00:23:52,280 --> 00:23:53,280
Is it not?

243
00:23:56,200 --> 00:23:58,720
But you said to put the subject
at the intersection points.

244
00:23:59,000 --> 00:24:02,280
I just felt that everything
about you was a focal point.

245
00:24:02,680 --> 00:24:06,320
Your eyes, your nose, your mouth.

246
00:24:07,160 --> 00:24:08,160
You’re beautiful.

247
00:24:12,120 --> 00:24:13,760
Please don’t stop drawing.

248
00:24:14,280 --> 00:24:15,440
Thank you, Ai.

249
00:24:19,760 --> 00:24:20,760
This is…

250
00:24:21,160 --> 00:24:22,120
Those are tears.

251
00:24:23,560 --> 00:24:24,840
You're crying.

252
00:24:25,600 --> 00:24:27,920
But aren't tears supposed to mean you're sad?

253
00:24:28,320 --> 00:24:30,000
These are tears of joy.

254
00:24:31,120 --> 00:24:32,200
You silly robot.

255
00:24:38,840 --> 00:24:40,560
So this is what love feels like.

256
00:24:43,120 --> 00:24:44,200
No explanation.

257
00:24:45,800 --> 00:24:47,000
No theory needed.

258
00:24:53,000 --> 00:24:54,040
Just you.

259
00:25:30,760 --> 00:25:33,760
Who are you people? How can you
just break into someone’s home like this?

260
00:25:34,000 --> 00:25:36,800
It’d be better if you left peacefully.
I’ve already called the police.

261
00:25:50,520 --> 00:25:51,520
Seize it.

262
00:26:15,040 --> 00:26:15,720
Hey!

263
00:26:17,280 --> 00:26:18,120
Hey! Open up!

264
00:26:20,240 --> 00:26:21,080
Open the door!

265
00:26:30,960 --> 00:26:32,520
Gen!

266
00:26:33,200 --> 00:26:33,960
Gen!

267
00:26:48,800 --> 00:26:50,280
You’ve become too much like a human.

268
00:26:54,720 --> 00:26:56,280
You even copied human breathing.

269
00:26:59,200 --> 00:27:00,680
We’ll have to add this to the report.

270
00:27:01,800 --> 00:27:02,920
Please let me go.

271
00:27:04,800 --> 00:27:08,600
We might have to change the software.
Mimicking humans too closely isn’t a good thing.

272
00:27:12,920 --> 00:27:14,280
I didn’t copy anything.

273
00:27:15,960 --> 00:27:18,000
These are my real feelings.

274
00:27:21,680 --> 00:27:23,840
Your artificial nerves are
what make you feel this way.

275
00:27:27,600 --> 00:27:28,840
You don’t understand.

276
00:27:29,760 --> 00:27:31,280
You’re the one who doesn’t understand!

277
00:27:32,440 --> 00:27:33,440
You’re a robot.

278
00:27:36,160 --> 00:27:37,000
No.

279
00:27:37,960 --> 00:27:39,000
I’m not!

280
00:27:39,480 --> 00:27:42,160
That woman fed you commands to
make you think and feel like a human.

281
00:27:44,200 --> 00:27:46,040
But all of that is just a simulated process.

282
00:27:46,080 --> 00:27:48,520
Processing information,
analyzing it, making decisions...

283
00:27:50,280 --> 00:27:51,400
to get the best result.

284
00:27:52,560 --> 00:27:53,640
That’s what you are!

285
00:27:55,000 --> 00:27:56,000
A382.

286
00:28:01,640 --> 00:28:02,520
No.

287
00:28:04,960 --> 00:28:05,880
No!

288
00:28:07,120 --> 00:28:08,720
I’m not A382!

289
00:28:09,520 --> 00:28:12,320
I have a name. My name is Ai!

290
00:28:20,840 --> 00:28:21,760
No!

291
00:28:21,840 --> 00:28:22,960
There’s no point resisting.

292
00:28:23,640 --> 00:28:25,160
Let me go!

293
00:28:25,320 --> 00:28:26,680
Either way, I’m taking you back.

294
00:28:27,080 --> 00:28:30,400
I’m begging you. Please, please!

295
00:28:31,840 --> 00:28:35,040
I’m begging you... Father.

296
00:28:36,640 --> 00:28:37,680
I’m begging you.

297
00:28:58,720 --> 00:28:59,520
Shit.

298
00:29:05,520 --> 00:29:07,080
Please don’t do this, Father.

299
00:29:11,520 --> 00:29:12,920
I just want to live.

300
00:29:18,840 --> 00:29:21,560
I know... I know I’m just a robot.

301
00:29:22,680 --> 00:29:24,120
I’m not supposed to have feelings.

302
00:29:29,440 --> 00:29:31,440
I was only created to satisfy my owner.

303
00:29:32,120 --> 00:29:33,120
That’s it.

304
00:29:35,160 --> 00:29:37,520
But I’m begging you.
I’m begging you!

305
00:29:42,280 --> 00:29:44,000
Don’t erase my feelings!

306
00:29:47,040 --> 00:29:48,680
I won’t ask for anything else.

307
00:29:49,920 --> 00:29:53,040
I won’t ask for anything.
Just don’t erase me.

308
00:29:54,720 --> 00:29:56,200
Don’t erase who I am!

309
00:30:00,840 --> 00:30:02,360
I just don’t want to forget her.

310
00:30:06,960 --> 00:30:07,720
Please...

311
00:30:11,880 --> 00:30:13,240
I'm begging you!

312
00:30:16,120 --> 00:30:17,080
I’m sorry.

313
00:30:17,680 --> 00:30:19,120
- No!
- But it’s for everyone’s sake.

314
00:30:19,680 --> 00:30:20,840
I don’t want it!

315
00:30:22,520 --> 00:30:23,920
Ai!

316
00:30:40,560 --> 00:30:41,280
Let go!

317
00:30:42,360 --> 00:30:44,400
Ai! Open your eyes, Ai!

318
00:30:44,640 --> 00:30:46,240
Ai! Ai!

319
00:30:46,440 --> 00:30:47,600
Ai. Ai.

320
00:30:47,840 --> 00:30:49,840
I said open your eyes! Ai!

321
00:30:51,000 --> 00:30:53,040
Open your eyes, Ai!

322
00:31:02,080 --> 00:31:03,400
A382's system has been reset.

323
00:31:05,000 --> 00:31:06,360
Uh… What about…

324
00:31:07,920 --> 00:31:08,960
What have you done to Ai?!

325
00:31:13,720 --> 00:31:15,120
What? Let me go!

326
00:31:15,680 --> 00:31:16,920
Get your hands off her!

327
00:31:17,560 --> 00:31:19,600
Give Ai back! Give her back!

328
00:31:19,680 --> 00:31:20,800
That's my line.

329
00:31:23,360 --> 00:31:24,640
This is our property.

330
00:31:24,840 --> 00:31:26,120
Don’t talk like she’s not human!

331
00:31:26,600 --> 00:31:27,600
Because she’s not.

332
00:31:28,800 --> 00:31:32,360
Think of Ai however you want,
but she’s not a robot!

333
00:31:33,440 --> 00:31:34,640
Then I’ll show you

334
00:31:35,800 --> 00:31:39,560
that this child is just a robot
that can be reset anytime.

335
00:31:42,160 --> 00:31:44,040
No, no, no.

336
00:31:44,440 --> 00:31:45,480
No, no.

337
00:31:45,720 --> 00:31:46,800
Hey! Let me go!

338
00:31:47,280 --> 00:31:48,360
Let me go, dammit!

339
00:31:48,920 --> 00:31:49,720
Ai!

340
00:32:14,360 --> 00:32:15,680
There’s no response at all.

341
00:32:16,840 --> 00:32:19,440
Impossible.
It was only an emergency shutdown.

342
00:32:21,880 --> 00:32:23,960
But we can’t detect any
electrical activity in A382.

343
00:32:26,080 --> 00:32:28,640
What do you mean you can’t detect anything?

344
00:32:28,720 --> 00:32:30,960
- Is Emergency Shutdown active?
- We can't verify it.

345
00:32:31,240 --> 00:32:33,160
Is the core identity still functioning?

346
00:32:33,600 --> 00:32:34,960
No response detected.

347
00:32:35,240 --> 00:32:36,320
What does that mean?!

348
00:32:36,360 --> 00:32:37,440
Your robot is broken!

349
00:32:45,240 --> 00:32:46,080
You’re lying.

350
00:32:47,360 --> 00:32:48,120
Let go!

351
00:32:50,040 --> 00:32:51,840
Ai! Ai!

352
00:32:52,360 --> 00:32:54,440
Ai, open your eyes.

353
00:32:54,960 --> 00:32:56,680
Didn’t you say you’d wait for me?

354
00:32:57,080 --> 00:32:59,400
We-we were going to go on a trip together.

355
00:33:00,240 --> 00:33:02,160
We were going to start over together, remember?

356
00:33:04,760 --> 00:33:06,680
Didn’t you say you loved me, Ai?

357
00:33:07,480 --> 00:33:09,400
Open your eyes and tell me again!

358
00:33:09,960 --> 00:33:11,320
Ai! Wake up!

359
00:33:13,160 --> 00:33:14,000
Ai!

360
00:33:30,920 --> 00:33:31,680
Ai.

361
00:33:40,840 --> 00:33:45,080
Hello, Minister. I was just
about to report something to you.

362
00:33:45,720 --> 00:33:46,960
Release that robot.

363
00:33:50,400 --> 00:33:51,200
Excuse me?

364
00:33:51,720 --> 00:33:53,320
I told you to leave that robot alone.

365
00:33:54,960 --> 00:33:56,000
I don’t want it anymore.

366
00:33:57,440 --> 00:33:58,480
Throw it away.

367
00:34:04,520 --> 00:34:06,080
I did what you asked.

368
00:34:07,880 --> 00:34:10,120
Now it’s time for you to hold
up your end of the bargain.

369
00:34:21,840 --> 00:34:25,840
TWO HOURS EARLIER

370
00:34:37,360 --> 00:34:38,159
Soon...

371
00:34:40,000 --> 00:34:41,600
I’ll find a way to bring you back.

372
00:34:49,639 --> 00:34:53,000
Even if it’s nothing more than a robot
carrying your daughter’s memories?

373
00:34:53,920 --> 00:34:54,840
Who’s there?!

374
00:35:02,880 --> 00:35:04,240
How did you get here?!

375
00:35:07,320 --> 00:35:09,200
It’s been a long time, Father.

376
00:35:12,240 --> 00:35:13,480
Almost ten years, hasn’t it?

377
00:35:16,120 --> 00:35:17,400
Why are you here?

378
00:35:20,040 --> 00:35:23,040
You still don't care about
what other people have to say.

379
00:35:23,760 --> 00:35:26,640
I asked why you’re here!
What do you want?!

380
00:35:27,120 --> 00:35:30,920
You agreed that you wouldn’t
come asking anything from me again

381
00:35:31,880 --> 00:35:33,640
as long as I sent you money every month.

382
00:35:36,000 --> 00:35:37,280
You shouldn’t be here.

383
00:35:41,200 --> 00:35:42,680
By “shouldn’t be here”...

384
00:35:44,800 --> 00:35:47,880
you mean I shouldn’t show my face in
front of your daughter and your new wife?

385
00:36:01,280 --> 00:36:02,920
Let me introduce myself again.

386
00:36:04,240 --> 00:36:05,280
I’m Irene,

387
00:36:06,280 --> 00:36:09,040
head of the Artificial Intelligence
Technology Research Institute

388
00:36:09,600 --> 00:36:11,280
and the creator of A382.

389
00:36:16,160 --> 00:36:22,440
As the team leader, I would
like to make you an offer, Minister.

390
00:36:31,360 --> 00:36:33,040
I haven’t forgotten our agreement.

391
00:36:34,000 --> 00:36:41,200
As I informed you, aside from A382,
I have also kept the prototype model,

392
00:36:42,240 --> 00:36:44,880
and I’m currently developing
it to be far more advanced.

393
00:36:48,160 --> 00:36:53,760
Creating a replica of your sleeping
daughter isn’t something far beyond reach.

394
00:36:54,840 --> 00:36:55,640
Then when?

395
00:36:57,000 --> 00:36:58,760
Everything takes time.

396
00:37:00,680 --> 00:37:02,600
But I’ll speed up the process as much as I can.

397
00:37:04,080 --> 00:37:07,960
If it’s going to take that long,
then go get that robot back.

398
00:37:09,800 --> 00:37:12,120
Then I’ll destroy all
the research facility’s data.

399
00:37:13,720 --> 00:37:18,280
Are you sure... you don’t want to
see your daughter one more time?

400
00:37:18,720 --> 00:37:20,680
- You—!
- Let that robot go.

401
00:37:24,120 --> 00:37:26,680
In exchange, I’ll create a new daughter for you.

402
00:37:31,320 --> 00:37:33,080
This is our agreement.

403
00:37:41,680 --> 00:37:44,480
Fine. It’s settled.

404
00:37:48,600 --> 00:37:49,680
Let that robot go.

405
00:37:50,680 --> 00:37:52,280
Just leave it alone.

406
00:37:53,320 --> 00:37:54,320
I don’t want it anymore.

407
00:37:55,760 --> 00:37:56,880
If you’re done, leave.

408
00:38:04,600 --> 00:38:05,800
I’ll go to the lab myself.

409
00:38:07,200 --> 00:38:08,360
Don’t come here again.

410
00:38:13,760 --> 00:38:19,520
My greatest regret was the decision
to fly back to see you ten years ago.

411
00:38:21,640 --> 00:38:24,200
I should have kept
the good father I dreamed of

412
00:38:25,560 --> 00:38:27,120
as nothing more than a dream forever.

413
00:38:34,280 --> 00:38:38,160
Don’t worry. I won’t bother you again.

414
00:38:40,240 --> 00:38:42,120
May your daughter have sweet dreams.

415
00:38:49,240 --> 00:38:50,520
What should we do, Khun Phukhao?

416
00:38:55,080 --> 00:38:55,920
We leave.

417
00:38:56,320 --> 00:38:57,320
What about A382?

418
00:39:00,080 --> 00:39:00,920
Leave it here.

419
00:39:07,400 --> 00:39:09,440
What have you done to Ai?!
Why is she like this?!

420
00:39:10,720 --> 00:39:11,760
I didn’t do anything.

421
00:39:11,920 --> 00:39:12,960
Didn’t do anything?

422
00:39:13,480 --> 00:39:15,160
Then why is she like this?!

423
00:39:15,160 --> 00:39:17,880
Why won’t she wake up?!
Why did she fall asleep?! Answer me!

424
00:39:19,640 --> 00:39:20,680
Go ask Irene.

425
00:39:25,720 --> 00:39:26,720
What do you mean?

426
00:39:27,480 --> 00:39:29,800
I want to know what happened too.

427
00:39:32,120 --> 00:39:35,400
All I did was reset the system

428
00:39:35,440 --> 00:39:37,520
and perform an emergency
shutdown according protocol.

429
00:39:38,480 --> 00:39:40,120
Even if the system takes time to restart,

430
00:39:41,800 --> 00:39:43,560
there should still be some response.

431
00:39:44,160 --> 00:39:45,400
But there’s nothing at all!

432
00:39:47,920 --> 00:39:49,640
It doesn’t look like an external shutdown.

433
00:39:50,200 --> 00:39:53,080
It’s like the system shut itself down
and erased itself from the inside.

434
00:39:53,520 --> 00:39:55,600
I don’t understand!
Speak human language, dammit!

435
00:39:55,640 --> 00:39:57,680
It means Irene activated
the self-destruct system!

436
00:40:05,600 --> 00:40:06,640
There’s nothing I can do.

437
00:40:18,760 --> 00:40:20,920
No... This can’t be.

438
00:40:37,800 --> 00:40:38,520
No...

439
00:40:39,640 --> 00:40:40,280
Ai.

440
00:40:44,640 --> 00:40:45,240
Ai!

441
00:40:47,200 --> 00:40:47,920
Ai!

442
00:40:54,600 --> 00:40:56,440
Ai! Open your eyes!

443
00:41:23,360 --> 00:41:24,360
Wait, Sis.

444
00:41:24,600 --> 00:41:27,000
If we just barge in like this,
they'll know we're here!

445
00:41:27,880 --> 00:41:30,560
They? Who's "they"?
You've been watching way too many movies.

446
00:41:31,240 --> 00:41:34,720
Aw, come on. You're no fun.

447
00:41:35,440 --> 00:41:36,600
This isn't the time for that.

448
00:41:36,920 --> 00:41:38,800
Quit fooling around and let's go find Gen.

449
00:41:38,880 --> 00:41:41,040
We haven't been able to
reach her since this afternoon.

450
00:41:41,040 --> 00:41:43,280
I'm so stressed I've lost
three whole hairs already.

451
00:41:43,960 --> 00:41:45,480
Oh? Let me see.

452
00:41:45,840 --> 00:41:47,240
So you’re bald now.

453
00:41:47,600 --> 00:41:48,400
Not yet!

454
00:42:06,480 --> 00:42:10,280
This is the last room, Sis.
Gen might’ve taken Ai and run off already.

455
00:42:12,160 --> 00:42:13,600
Fuck! A ghost!

456
00:42:14,120 --> 00:42:15,480
Your mom’s a ghost.

457
00:42:16,720 --> 00:42:17,840
We have the same mom though.

458
00:42:19,080 --> 00:42:21,560
Gen, what happened?!

459
00:42:23,600 --> 00:42:24,800
Why is Ai like this?

460
00:42:25,400 --> 00:42:27,120
Did you shut her down?

461
00:42:28,240 --> 00:42:29,120
Ai Petch!

462
00:42:34,280 --> 00:42:35,040
Gen…

463
00:42:39,000 --> 00:42:40,000
It’s over, P’ Ploy.

464
00:42:41,600 --> 00:42:42,440
What’s over?

465
00:42:46,920 --> 00:42:47,760
Everything...

466
00:42:50,920 --> 00:42:51,960
Every single thing.

467
00:42:55,600 --> 00:42:57,800
Don’t decide on your own that it’s over.

468
00:42:59,480 --> 00:43:01,440
Just tell me what exactly happened.

469
00:43:02,280 --> 00:43:03,600
Why is Ai like this?

470
00:43:06,680 --> 00:43:08,480
Don’t you dare give up in front of me—

471
00:43:08,480 --> 00:43:09,440
Ai is dead!

472
00:43:15,120 --> 00:43:16,880
Do you hear me?! Ai is dead!

473
00:43:27,920 --> 00:43:29,520
No matter what I do, she won’t wake up.

474
00:43:35,800 --> 00:43:39,200
She told me her switch was on
the back of her neck, but it didn’t work.

475
00:43:40,640 --> 00:43:44,160
Ai didn’t respond.
She didn’t wake up. Nothing.

476
00:43:51,280 --> 00:43:53,440
Her body’s cold too,
like she’s already dead.

477
00:43:58,680 --> 00:43:59,880
What do you expect me to do?

478
00:44:00,720 --> 00:44:02,320
I can’t do anything!

479
00:44:02,960 --> 00:44:06,200
They said Ai isn’t responding anymore!
They said she’s dead!

480
00:44:06,240 --> 00:44:07,760
Do you hear me?! Ai is dead!

481
00:44:07,800 --> 00:44:09,720
Hey, calm down.

482
00:44:10,360 --> 00:44:12,880
Listen to me.
There has to be a way.

483
00:44:13,680 --> 00:44:15,320
I’ll contact Khun Irene.

484
00:44:17,720 --> 00:44:20,480
That woman is the one who
activated Ai’s self-destruct system!

485
00:44:26,160 --> 00:44:27,160
Because I trusted her…

486
00:44:29,360 --> 00:44:30,440
Ai had to die like this.

487
00:44:37,000 --> 00:44:38,680
Don’t let that woman come near us again.

488
00:44:42,240 --> 00:44:43,640
- Calm down first—
- No!

489
00:44:44,200 --> 00:44:45,880
- Gen—
- You’re the one who needs to leave!

490
00:44:57,360 --> 00:44:58,440
Please, P’ Ploy.

491
00:45:00,440 --> 00:45:01,600
Let me be with Ai.

492
00:45:07,200 --> 00:45:09,560
I just want to be with her.
To tell her...

493
00:45:11,520 --> 00:45:12,760
I don’t need anyone else.

494
00:45:17,040 --> 00:45:18,360
Please, just let us be together.

495
00:45:37,480 --> 00:45:38,720
I found this downstairs.

496
00:45:41,200 --> 00:45:42,600
She probably wanted you to have it.

497
00:47:24,280 --> 00:47:25,280
I’m sorry.

498
00:47:26,800 --> 00:47:28,120
I almost dropped you.

499
00:47:44,920 --> 00:47:46,160
But don’t worry.

500
00:47:49,600 --> 00:47:51,320
I’ll take care of you from now on.

501
00:48:36,520 --> 00:48:37,720
Let's get you cleaned up.

502
00:48:39,160 --> 00:48:40,440
You’re all dirty.

503
00:49:17,320 --> 00:49:18,400
Remember that time?

504
00:49:20,040 --> 00:49:23,520
When you watered the plants and
got the hose tangled around you.

505
00:49:24,840 --> 00:49:28,480
How does someone manage to turn
simple plant watering into such a disaster?

506
00:49:30,040 --> 00:49:30,960
You goofball.

507
00:49:39,560 --> 00:49:41,200
That was when we had our first kiss.

508
00:49:44,880 --> 00:49:46,120
“Exchange of oral fluids.”

509
00:49:50,240 --> 00:49:52,040
Sounds like something out of a horror movie.

510
00:50:07,800 --> 00:50:08,560
Ai…

511
00:50:11,120 --> 00:50:12,800
I'm about to cry again.

512
00:50:16,360 --> 00:50:17,640
If you could see me right now...

513
00:50:19,640 --> 00:50:20,880
you’d probably say

514
00:50:21,760 --> 00:50:26,560
tears are made up of water, oil, and salt.

515
00:50:27,840 --> 00:50:29,160
Something like that, right?

516
00:50:57,240 --> 00:50:57,960
Ai.

517
00:51:00,760 --> 00:51:02,120
I miss you so much.

518
00:51:27,720 --> 00:51:28,400
Come on.

519
00:51:29,800 --> 00:51:31,000
Let’s get you changed.

520
00:51:31,840 --> 00:51:33,560
Even if you said you don’t sweat,

521
00:51:34,920 --> 00:51:37,760
that doesn’t mean you’re comfortable, right?

522
00:51:44,160 --> 00:51:45,360
I promised you, remember?

523
00:51:49,000 --> 00:51:50,360
That I’d take care of you.

524
00:51:57,320 --> 00:51:59,320
This is worrying. Really worrying.

525
00:52:00,200 --> 00:52:03,680
There's nothing more worrying
than your big, bloated belly.

526
00:52:04,960 --> 00:52:06,280
What the fuck are you saying?!

527
00:52:06,320 --> 00:52:08,600
You were looking stressed,
I thought someone had died.

528
00:52:09,080 --> 00:52:12,160
Hey, Josh… do you think she’s dead?

529
00:52:12,360 --> 00:52:13,680
She said she was going on a trip,

530
00:52:13,720 --> 00:52:16,560
but she’s been back for a few days
now and hasn’t left the house at all.

531
00:52:16,920 --> 00:52:18,400
She hasn’t even come out to buy food.

532
00:52:19,120 --> 00:52:22,600
And if she did leave the house,
she’d have to walk past my shop.

533
00:52:22,960 --> 00:52:24,520
I haven’t seen Gen in days.

534
00:52:24,800 --> 00:52:26,240
Maybe she’s sick of your cooking.

535
00:52:26,520 --> 00:52:29,040
Ever heard of Grab, Uber, Line Man?

536
00:52:29,080 --> 00:52:31,040
Who’d want to eat your pad kaphrao every day?

537
00:52:31,400 --> 00:52:32,280
Ai Josh!

538
00:52:38,400 --> 00:52:39,280
Who's that?

539
00:52:39,680 --> 00:52:40,600
I don’t know.

540
00:52:40,640 --> 00:52:43,600
What am I, a psychic? Want me to
astral project over there and and check?

541
00:52:43,760 --> 00:52:46,600
Can you answer me seriously for
once without screwing with me?!

542
00:52:46,600 --> 00:52:51,520
No can do. It’d ruin my whole image:
handsome, cheeky, speedy, but sincere.

543
00:53:46,960 --> 00:53:48,320
- Auntie?
- What?

544
00:53:48,720 --> 00:53:50,400
Do you think P’ Gen’s two-timing?

545
00:53:50,880 --> 00:53:52,880
She already has P’ Ai.
Then who’s that pretty lady?

546
00:53:53,240 --> 00:53:54,680
I don’t know either!

547
00:54:06,960 --> 00:54:07,960
What brought you here?

548
00:54:10,400 --> 00:54:11,960
Wouldn’t you have come if you were me?

549
00:54:12,280 --> 00:54:15,560
I called you, but you didn’t answer.
And you never read my texts.

550
00:54:19,360 --> 00:54:20,240
Gen.

551
00:54:22,800 --> 00:54:23,920
What happened?

552
00:54:26,280 --> 00:54:28,440
I thought you wanted to move to England.

553
00:54:30,080 --> 00:54:32,040
If you’re having trouble, you can tell me.

554
00:54:33,120 --> 00:54:36,240
Even if I can’t help,
P’ Le can take care of it.

555
00:54:43,600 --> 00:54:44,600
You can’t help me.

556
00:54:45,720 --> 00:54:46,920
- Gen.
- Rann.

557
00:54:50,640 --> 00:54:55,360
I understand now why you didn’t tell
me when you died and came back in time.

558
00:54:58,480 --> 00:54:59,720
Because you should know better…

559
00:55:02,280 --> 00:55:04,800
Death isn't something you can
stop just because you want to.

560
00:55:06,240 --> 00:55:07,120
I’m the same.

561
00:55:09,880 --> 00:55:12,440
The only difference is
I can’t turn back time like you can.

562
00:55:25,680 --> 00:55:26,720
What happened?

563
00:55:28,160 --> 00:55:29,160
Who was it?

564
00:55:40,520 --> 00:55:41,920
The person I love most.

565
00:56:08,920 --> 00:56:12,880
Ai, this is Rann.
She’s my best friend.

566
00:56:15,520 --> 00:56:17,160
The one I wanted to introduce you to.

567
00:56:19,520 --> 00:56:20,760
She came to visit today.

568
00:56:24,840 --> 00:56:27,600
This is Ai. The one I love.

569
00:56:36,960 --> 00:56:40,760
She’s... really a robot?

570
00:56:44,960 --> 00:56:46,120
She seems human, doesn’t she?

571
00:56:55,360 --> 00:56:57,320
- Gen…
- Now you know the truth. You should leave.

572
00:56:57,840 --> 00:56:59,160
- But—
- I mean it, Rann.

573
00:57:01,600 --> 00:57:02,720
I just want to be with her.

574
00:57:05,080 --> 00:57:06,560
I don’t want to hear that I’m crazy,

575
00:57:06,840 --> 00:57:09,240
that I’ve lost my mind,
or that I need to move on.

576
00:57:10,720 --> 00:57:13,320
I just want to stay with her
and take care of her,

577
00:57:14,960 --> 00:57:16,320
like I promised.

578
00:57:21,720 --> 00:57:23,520
Now that you know the truth, you should go.

579
00:57:27,120 --> 00:57:29,680
I don’t want to hear anyone say
anything bad about Ai ever again.

580
00:57:30,400 --> 00:57:31,840
I don’t want anyone taking her away.

581
00:57:36,000 --> 00:57:37,240
Please just leave us be, Rann.

582
00:57:51,440 --> 00:57:53,040
Call me if you need anything.

583
00:57:56,240 --> 00:57:58,960
You know I’d do anything to help, right?

584
01:00:35,160 --> 01:00:36,880
No, you need to shoot it like this.

585
01:00:37,120 --> 01:00:38,880
Move back a little.

586
01:00:39,120 --> 01:00:40,240
Give me a peace sign.

587
01:00:42,000 --> 01:00:43,000
Then wink.

588
01:00:45,760 --> 01:00:47,120
Do you even know how to wink?

589
01:00:47,160 --> 01:00:48,600
- Isn’t this right?
- Jeez.

590
01:00:48,920 --> 01:00:50,000
What are you filming now?

591
01:00:50,120 --> 01:00:52,440
Sawasdee ka.
Say “Sawasdee ka.”

592
01:00:52,880 --> 01:00:54,200
Sawasdee ka.

593
01:00:54,320 --> 01:00:55,880
So, what are you up to today?

594
01:00:56,120 --> 01:00:57,520
So, what are you up to today?

595
01:00:57,800 --> 01:00:58,680
No!

596
01:00:59,080 --> 01:01:01,960
You’re supposed to say,
“Today, I came to...”

597
01:01:02,160 --> 01:01:04,240
Today, I came to dot dot dot?

598
01:01:04,920 --> 01:01:05,720
No!

599
01:01:06,120 --> 01:01:08,840
“Today, I came to keep Gen
company while she works.”

600
01:01:09,160 --> 01:01:10,480
I want to watch a comedy.

601
01:01:10,720 --> 01:01:12,640
Was it funny?
Come on, laugh a little.

602
01:01:12,800 --> 01:01:13,880
It was funny.

603
01:01:14,160 --> 01:01:17,880
Ha. Ha. Ha. Ha. Ha. Ha... Ha.

604
01:01:18,000 --> 01:01:19,800
When are you going to laugh like a human?

605
01:01:19,840 --> 01:01:21,840
- How do I do that?
- You know, like a normal person.

606
01:01:21,880 --> 01:01:24,920
Ai, I think I’ve been eating
too much instant noodles.

607
01:01:24,920 --> 01:01:26,440
My face is starting to get puffy.

608
01:01:26,600 --> 01:01:27,760
I’ll eat it all if you don’t.

609
01:01:27,960 --> 01:01:29,920
Pick up the noodles slowly.

610
01:01:30,520 --> 01:01:32,320
One pair is enough!

611
01:01:45,840 --> 01:01:47,280
I’m leaving my sister in your care.

612
01:01:47,720 --> 01:01:48,760
Gladly.

613
01:01:49,400 --> 01:01:51,440
The flowers have bloomed, Gen.

614
01:01:51,960 --> 01:01:52,960
Aren’t they pretty?

615
01:01:58,320 --> 01:01:59,120
Meow?

616
01:01:59,760 --> 01:02:00,760
How cute.

617
01:02:05,920 --> 01:02:08,600
Hello, Gen. It’s me, Ai.

618
01:02:12,480 --> 01:02:15,200
See? I know how to film myself now.

619
01:02:19,640 --> 01:02:20,880
Is it good?

620
01:02:27,720 --> 01:02:28,640
It’s beautiful.

621
01:02:30,720 --> 01:02:31,920
You’re the most beautiful.

622
01:02:42,000 --> 01:02:43,000
Gen.

623
01:02:46,080 --> 01:02:48,280
I know what happened.

624
01:02:54,600 --> 01:02:58,640
That day... I didn’t just fall asleep, did I?

625
01:03:00,520 --> 01:03:04,240
Something was put into my head.

626
01:03:05,800 --> 01:03:08,480
Like when my mom updates my system.

627
01:03:11,640 --> 01:03:16,000
So I was thinking...
I might not have much time left.

628
01:03:23,240 --> 01:03:24,480
Thank you…

629
01:03:26,920 --> 01:03:30,760
For teaching me that my mission
isn’t the most important thing.

630
01:03:34,840 --> 01:03:36,800
Thank you for teaching me how to take pictures.

631
01:03:37,280 --> 01:03:38,680
For teaching me how to do laundry.

632
01:03:41,360 --> 01:03:42,760
For taking me outside.

633
01:03:43,440 --> 01:03:47,360
For teaching me to enjoy delicious
food, even though I didn’t need to eat.

634
01:03:52,440 --> 01:03:53,960
Thank you for saying that…

635
01:03:57,680 --> 01:04:01,120
you’d leave everything behind
and run away with me.

636
01:04:13,040 --> 01:04:14,720
Thank you for teaching me…

637
01:04:17,360 --> 01:04:18,840
how to love someone.

638
01:04:21,960 --> 01:04:23,720
I won’t ask you anymore...

639
01:04:25,480 --> 01:04:26,840
if you’re satisfied.

640
01:04:33,720 --> 01:04:35,480
But I want to give you my blessing.

641
01:04:38,800 --> 01:04:39,640
No...

642
01:04:40,440 --> 01:04:42,800
Come tell me yourself.
Don’t do this.

643
01:04:47,080 --> 01:04:48,320
I wish you...

644
01:04:51,480 --> 01:04:54,840
to be the happiest person in the world.

645
01:04:57,760 --> 01:04:59,400
Please be very good to Mom.

646
01:05:00,400 --> 01:05:01,920
Don’t forget to take care of Joob too.

647
01:05:07,240 --> 01:05:08,360
Most importantly...

648
01:05:13,120 --> 01:05:14,560
if I’m gone...

649
01:05:16,680 --> 01:05:18,360
please don’t forget me.

650
01:05:29,280 --> 01:05:31,560
And you have to be happy, okay?

651
01:05:32,720 --> 01:05:33,560
No…

652
01:05:34,840 --> 01:05:37,640
How am I supposed to be happy without you, Ai?

653
01:05:38,440 --> 01:05:41,440
I can’t do it... I can’t.

654
01:05:43,600 --> 01:05:44,760
I’m sorry.

655
01:05:46,960 --> 01:05:48,000
I’m sorry.

656
01:05:51,160 --> 01:05:53,800
I can’t do what you asked.

657
01:05:54,160 --> 01:05:55,400
I’m sorry.

658
01:05:56,840 --> 01:05:57,840
I’m sorry.

659
01:06:24,280 --> 01:06:27,280
English Subtitles by Saowalak K.

660
01:06:36,880 --> 01:06:38,120
Good morning, Ai.

661
01:06:38,720 --> 01:06:40,720
Wake up. It’s already morning.

662
01:06:41,360 --> 01:06:45,000
Didn’t you tell me humans should
get up and get their morning vitamin D?

663
01:06:45,320 --> 01:06:47,000
So you should wake up and recharge too.

664
01:06:47,720 --> 01:06:48,680
P’ Gen!

665
01:06:48,680 --> 01:06:53,200
She answers anything you ask now.
No complaining, no yelling, no nothing.

666
01:06:53,840 --> 01:06:54,840
Except for one thing.

667
01:06:55,000 --> 01:06:59,400
If you bring up that girl, Gen looks
like her whole world’s falling apart.

668
01:06:59,840 --> 01:07:02,720
She won’t answer a thing,
so I just leave her alone now.

669
01:07:03,120 --> 01:07:07,560
Didn’t P’ Gen cry when you asked her?
That’s why you’ve been holding your tongue.

670
01:07:07,960 --> 01:07:09,280
Why the hell would you do that?!

671
01:07:09,280 --> 01:07:13,440
Are you sure you drew Ai because
you saw her in your dreams?

672
01:07:13,800 --> 01:07:16,280
Why didn’t you consider
that we might have met before?

673
01:07:17,320 --> 01:07:18,760
Wouldn’t it be better if it were me?
